n":"supersedes","target_id":"31a7-371a-0f1c-403d"},{"link_uuid":"84001322-d7cc-4c8c-8610-859597cc4169","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a77c-69ee-09b4-4887"},{"link_uuid":"50afc6cc-d4c8-4445-98b9-4d877abef7d2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"26ac-5d5b-51ea-48df"},{"link_uuid":"a4219cd6-496c-49f9-b2e7-9709d56d006f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a0a7-4e98-c76a-4b2a"},{"link_uuid":"78207661-f782-43d9-a579-92f549734cf8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b864-8df4-87e5-4928"},{"link_uuid":"19357821-bd66-434b-afc6-add1ec2a4a61","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"02db-5761-afb0-4eef"},{"link_uuid":"ee84831e-77c1-40bb-bd0a-eca5d65cb2d9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b871-f488-491b-4e97"},{"link_uuid":"8ed8ff72-592a-478b-8cf2-3636811623de","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"73d4-405a-c3c2-4883"},{"link_uuid":"efa93f61-7a55-4e08-9283-b3481390d864","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"079f-be58-5f52-4f42"},{"link_uuid":"61cba681-3507-4213-87f4-9656a95820bf","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2233-2b89-71c9-442c"},{"link_uuid":"d593dc2e-0842-4be9-adcc-d91ef7f2189e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0f77-9351-dce0-41db"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/external/live_jira_dc cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_bridge_output.py:1-37` — Preserve canonical stream contract and distinction between convergence and zero writes. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py:1-27, 55-65, 105-120, 139-150, 168-178, 189-202, 212-215, 265-269, 279-283, 312-323` — Preserve fixture visibility, two-repository topology, environment snapshot, cache scrub, no-remotes isolation, and binding preconditions. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_support.py:1-14, 35-41, 45-53, 69-74, 84-94, 112-127, 159-163, 251-262, 281-298, 345-365, 427-436, 442-467, 486-493, 501-516, 560-577, 614-633, 669-690, 723-742` — Preserve vendor invariants, safety scope, exact-match oracles, eventual-consistency handling, and non-vacuity checks. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:1-17, 56-60, 67-76, 158-172, 190-215, 268-278, 298-316, 357-376, 379-383, 440-452, 464-471, 476-496, 516-530, 555-579, 600-607, 613-627, 634-638, 669-680, 695-712, 737-766, 781-787` — Preserve readiness, leak sweeps, scratch-project safety, field provisioning, teardown, and PAT lifecycle. Consumer: `tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py:69-71` requires the `jira_dc_pat` docstring at `737-766` to retain both “10” and “SESSION”.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/Dockerfile:30-64` — Preserve required working JVM properties, runtime-download fact, effective timeout, and citations. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py:1-34, 62-67, 163-174, 180-185, 398-406, 423-457, 461-464, 518-523, 634-661, 676-679, 748-777, 819-832, 844-861, 932-954, 1022-1029, 1135-1138, 1146-1167, 1206-1227, 1240-1246, 1287-1309, 1380-1400, 1426-1430, 1491-1498, 1527-1536, 1608-1651, 1700-1703, 1733-1759, 1868-1911, 1972-1977, 2002-2049, 2111-2121, 2148-2176, 2179-2183, 2231-2258, 2297-2339, 2447-2462, 2483-2493, 2549-2555, 2587-2602, 2610-2615` — Preserve each row’s setup, mutation, observable remote/local oracle, cleanup, and vendor-specific constraint. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_rich_text_live.py:1-32, 48-51, 61-71, 75-79, 108-118, 136-150, 181-184, 234-242, 293-307` — Preserve wire-format boundaries, direct-read diagnostics, conflict behavior, and observable round trips. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py:1-28, 409-412` — Preserve investigation-only semantics and structured-result contract. The tool descriptions at `209-215` and `232-238` are behavior-bearing LLM inputs and were intentionally not flagged. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_harness_smoke.py:1-27` — Preserve raw REST boundary, deployment/version assertion, PAT path, and cleanup. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py:1-39, 89-95, 183-191, 232-237, 251-271, 344-352, 466-469, 525-532, 578-590, 638-641, 668-676, 748-751` — Preserve structural isolation, preview-before-write, project-scope oracle, index waits, cleanup, and fail-closed cases. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py:1-36, 162-172, 257-261, 295-305` — Preserve completion, idempotence, provenance/binding, canonical-output, and exact derived-ID checks. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py:1-32, 53-58, 88-92, 98-101, 147-160, 197-204, 220-226, 240-248` — Preserve real-copy completeness, inherited-environment evidence, binding scrub, differ visibility, bidirectional proof, and no-push safety. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py:1-29, 79-86, 206-214, 295-310, 358-375, 470-490, 496-500, 592-620, 739-763, 802-811` — Preserve live vendor contract, identity resolution, full method coverage, stable numeric ID, permission measurement, and measured label ceiling. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_user_guide_commands.py:1-23, 108-115` — Preserve literal documentation-execution boundary, harness requirement, and security assertions. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest --collect-only tests/external/live_jira_dc/_bridge_output.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_support.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/Dockerfile tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_rich_text_live.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_harness_smoke.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_store_copy_isolation.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_user_guide_commands.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/_bridge_output.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_support.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py","reason":"Condense comment